{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121793","id":4136307504,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc72iwsw","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121793","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121793.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121793.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121793","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121793/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121793/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121793/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/b89e2a3c1d037c89743e7012e97443ffea945bfe","number":121793,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Change mentions of \"member\" to \"property\" where appropriate","user":{"login":"Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"\r\nSee also a [RocketChat discussion](https://chat.godotengine.org/channel/documentation/thread/tPE9nBS6iKFaX2WJm), if it were to embed properly.\r\n\r\nMany spots in the class reference say \"_member_\" when they either _really_ mean to say \"_property_\" or \"_member variable_\".\r\n\"Member\" is almost always incorrect for reasons explained below. But, there's a bunch of annoying nuance between \"property\" or \"member variable\".\r\nSo I did make up my mind and, **as far as Godot is concerned**, I think that:\r\n\r\n- A \"_member_\" is _anything_ belonging to an object ~~or class~~. Properties, signals, methods, constants, even inner classes, etc. are all members.\r\n\t- Local variables and local constants[^1] are **not** members.\r\n\t- This is not particularly controversial, but it's worth keeping in mind nonetheless.\r\n- A \"_member variable_\" is one type of member.\r\n- A \"_property_\" is:\r\n\t- A member variable declared **in GDScript** (with the `var` keyword in the class body).\r\n\t- A member variable exposed with `ADD_PROPERTY`\r\n\t- almost everything present in the array returned by `Object.get_property_list` (hold to that thought)\r\n\r\nFor most practical use-cases, what matters most is that a property is a member, but a member is **not always** a property. This distinction is very similar to \"method\" vs. \"function\".\r\nBut in some cases it is worth being more specific because, as the prior explanations imply:\r\n\r\n- A \"member variable\" points to an actual space in memory, so to speak.\r\n- A dynamic/custom/fake property be exposed via `Object._get_property_list` and similar methods\r\n\t- This means a property is oftentimes associated with a member variable, but that's **not always the case**.\r\n\r\n[Ideally a similar tweak should also be applied in `godot-docs`](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-docs/pull/12182)\r\n\r\nYes, the class reference's `member` tag is still named that way for legacy reasons.\r\n\r\n[^1]: I recall that local constants are not purely local, but this is an internal detail.","labels":[{"